# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The concepts in this guide are only available in the Python API.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Conceptele din acest ghid sunt disponibile doar în API-ul Python.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The local unitary cluster Jastrow ([LUCJ](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlelanding/2023/sc/d3sc02516k)) ansatz is a compact, hardware-efficient parametrization of a correlated electronic wavefunction. It is a member of the more general unitary cluster Jastrow (UCJ) family and takes the form\n"
msgstr "Ansatzul local unitary cluster Jastrow ([LUCJ](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlelanding/2023/sc/d3sc02516k)) este o parametrizare compactă, eficientă hardware, a unei funcții de undă electronice corelate. Este un membru al familiei mai generale unitary cluster Jastrow (UCJ) și are forma\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lvert \\Psi \\rangle = \\left(\\prod_{k=1}^{L} \\mathcal{U}_k\\, e^{i \\mathcal{J}_k}\\,\n"
"\\mathcal{U}_k^\\dagger\\right) \\lvert \\Phi_0 \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lvert \\Psi \\rangle = \\left(\\prod_{k=1}^{L} \\mathcal{U}_k\\, e^{i \\mathcal{J}_k}\\,\n"
"\\mathcal{U}_k^\\dagger\\right) \\lvert \\Phi_0 \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\lvert \\Phi_0 \\rangle$ is a reference state (typically Hartree-Fock), each $\\mathcal{U}_k$ is an orbital rotation, and each $\\mathcal{J}_k$ is a diagonal Coulomb operator\n"
msgstr "unde $\\lvert \\Phi_0 \\rangle$ este o stare de referință (de obicei Hartree-Fock), fiecare $\\mathcal{U}_k$ este o rotație orbitală, iar fiecare $\\mathcal{J}_k$ este un operator Coulomb diagonal\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{J} = \\frac12 \\sum_{ij,\\sigma\\tau} \\mathbf{J}^{\\sigma\\tau}_{ij}\\,\n"
"n_{i\\sigma}\\, n_{j\\tau},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{J} = \\frac12 \\sum_{ij,\\sigma\\tau} \\mathbf{J}^{\\sigma\\tau}_{ij}\\,\n"
"n_{i\\sigma}\\, n_{j\\tau},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with $n_{i\\sigma}$ the number operator on spatial orbital $i$ with spin $\\sigma$.\n"
msgstr "cu $n_{i\\sigma}$ operatorul de număr pe orbitalul spațial $i$ cu spinul $\\sigma$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) builds the ansatz operator; this package turns it into a circuit and lowers that circuit onto qubits. This guide is about the second half of that sentence. The reason to make the trip is the lowering itself: ffsim’s own Qiskit gates are specific to the Jordan-Wigner transformation, whereas a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") carries no assumption about its fermion-to-qubit encoding, so the same ansatz can be synthesized through whichever encoding suits the target device.\n"
msgstr "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) construiește operatorul ansatz; acest pachet îl transformă într-un circuit și coboară acel circuit pe qubiți. Acest ghid tratează a doua jumătate a acestei propoziții. Motivul pentru care merită să faci acest drum este chiar coborârea: porțile Qiskit proprii ale ffsim sunt specifice transformării Jordan-Wigner, în timp ce un [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") nu presupune nimic despre codificarea fermion-qubit, deci același ansatz poate fi sintetizat prin orice codificare potrivită dispozitivului țintă.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ansatz operator therefore arrives here ready-made, and everything below is what happens to it afterwards: what the gate decomposes into, how it lowers through Jordan-Wigner, how it is matched to a device coupling map, and what a non-Jordan-Wigner lowering would still need. For building, parametrizing, or simulating a UCJ ansatz in the first place, see ffsim’s [own guides](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/how-to-guides/qiskit-lucj.html).\n"
msgstr "Prin urmare, operatorul ansatz ajunge aici gata făcut, iar tot ce urmează este ce se întâmplă cu el după aceea: în ce se descompune poarta, cum coboară prin Jordan-Wigner, cum este potrivit pe o hartă de cuplare a dispozitivului și ce ar mai fi necesar pentru o coborâre non-Jordan-Wigner. Pentru construirea, parametrizarea sau simularea unui ansatz UCJ de la bun început, vezi [ghidurile proprii](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/how-to-guides/qiskit-lucj.html) ale ffsim.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"See also\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The [ffsim relationship guide](ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation) for how the two packages divide the work, and the [transpilation guide](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) for the pipeline stages used below.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Vezi și\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [Ghidul relației cu ffsim](ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation) pentru modul în care cele două pachete își împart munca și [ghidul de transpilare](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) pentru etapele pipeline-ului folosite mai jos.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"get-an-lucj-operator-from-ffsim\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Get an LUCJ operator from ffsim {#1-get-an-lucj-operator-from-ffsim}"
msgstr "1. Obține un operator LUCJ din ffsim {#1-get-an-lucj-operator-from-ffsim}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ansatz is initialized from the amplitudes of a coupled-cluster singles and doubles (CCSD) calculation. Run restricted Hartree-Fock followed by CCSD for a hydrogen molecule in the `6-31g` basis, using [PySCF](https://pyscf.org/) for the quantum chemistry, then hand the amplitudes to ffsim’s [`from_t_amplitudes()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.from_t_amplitudes \"(in ffsim)\"). It performs a *double factorization* of the $t_2$ amplitudes to obtain the per-layer diagonal Coulomb matrices and orbital rotations, and derives an optional final orbital rotation from the $t_1$ amplitudes. The number of repetitions $L$ is whatever that factorization yields; `n_reps` truncates it, trading accuracy for a shallower circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ansatzul este inițializat din amplitudinile unui calcul coupled-cluster cu simple și duble excitații (CCSD). Rulează Hartree-Fock restricționat urmat de CCSD pentru o moleculă de hidrogen în baza `6-31g`, folosind [PySCF](https://pyscf.org/) pentru chimia cuantică, apoi dă amplitudinile funcției [`from_t_amplitudes()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.from_t_amplitudes \"(in ffsim)\") din ffsim. Aceasta realizează o *factorizare dublă* a amplitudinilor $t_2$ pentru a obține matricile Coulomb diagonale și rotațiile orbitale pentru fiecare strat și deduce o rotație orbitală finală opțională din amplitudinile $t_1$. Numărul de repetări $L$ este cel pe care îl produce acea factorizare; `n_reps` îl trunchiază, schimbând acuratețea pe un circuit mai puțin adânc.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is where the ansatz stops being an ffsim concern. ffsim offers choices here that this package neither sees nor needs to know about, such as the variationally optimized (“compressed”) factorization behind `optimize=True`, or the parameter-vector packing that a variational optimizer drives. All of them produce the same kind of operator, and everything below works unchanged on any of them.\n"
msgstr "Aici ansatzul încetează să mai fie o preocupare a ffsim. ffsim oferă aici opțiuni pe care acest pachet nici nu le vede, nici nu trebuie să le cunoască, cum ar fi factorizarea („comprimată”) optimizată variațional din spatele lui `optimize=True` sau împachetarea vectorului de parametri pe care îl manipulează un optimizator variațional. Toate produc același tip de operator, iar tot ce urmează funcționează neschimbat pe oricare dintre ele.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"turn-the-operator-into-a-fermionic-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Turn the operator into a fermionic circuit {#2-turn-the-operator-into-a-fermionic-circuit}"
msgstr "2. Transformă operatorul într-un circuit fermionic {#2-turn-the-operator-into-a-fermionic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") gate wraps the operator and expresses it as a circuit over *fermionic modes*. The gate is a pure unitary carrying no reference of its own, so prepend an [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate (built with [`from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\")) to supply the Hartree-Fock reference the ansatz is applied to.\n"
msgstr "Poarta [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") înfășoară operatorul și îl exprimă ca un circuit peste *moduri fermionice*. Poarta este un unitar pur, fără nicio referință proprie, așa că adaugă la început o poartă [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") (construită cu [`from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\")) pentru a furniza referința Hartree-Fock căreia i se aplică ansatzul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Decomposing the circuit reveals its anatomy, and this is the representation the rest of the guide operates on. The [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate prepares the reference determinant, and each ansatz layer contributes an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") $\\mathcal{U}_k^\\dagger$, then $e^{i\\mathcal{J}_k}$ (an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") of the diagonal Coulomb operator $\\mathcal{J}_k$), then $\\mathcal{U}_k$, with a final [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") at the end. The orbital rotations act per spin sector, so each is placed on the alpha modes `0..norb` and the beta modes `norb..2*norb` independently.\n"
msgstr "Descompunerea circuitului îi dezvăluie anatomia și aceasta este reprezentarea pe care operează restul ghidului. Poarta [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") pregătește determinantul de referință, iar fiecare strat al ansatzului contribuie cu un [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") $\\mathcal{U}_k^\\dagger$, apoi $e^{i\\mathcal{J}_k}$ (un [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") al operatorului Coulomb diagonal $\\mathcal{J}_k$), apoi $\\mathcal{U}_k$, cu un [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") final la sfârșit. Rotațiile orbitale acționează pe fiecare sector de spin, deci fiecare este plasată independent pe modurile alfa `0..norb` și pe modurile beta `norb..2*norb`.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The gates that the UCJ ansatz decomposes into.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/lucj-3.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The gates that the UCJ ansatz decomposes into.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/lucj-3.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every gate in that decomposition is still fermionic: [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") and [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") are defined on modes, and no qubit or Pauli operator has appeared yet. That is what leaves the encoding open, and it is the state the ansatz stays in until the synthesis stage picks one.\n"
msgstr "Fiecare poartă din acea descompunere este încă fermionică: [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") și [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") sunt definite pe moduri și încă nu a apărut niciun operator de qubit sau Pauli. Aceasta lasă codificarea deschisă și este starea în care rămâne ansatzul până când etapa de sinteză alege una.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Each layer ends with $\\mathcal{U}_k$ and the next begins with $\\mathcal{U}_{k+1}^\\dagger$, so adjacent [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates could be merged into a single rotation. A transpilation pass performing this fusion is a planned future development.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Notă\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Fiecare strat se termină cu $\\mathcal{U}_k$, iar următorul începe cu $\\mathcal{U}_{k+1}^\\dagger$, deci porțile [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") adiacente ar putea fi îmbinate într-o singură rotație. Un pas de transpilare care realizează această fuziune este o dezvoltare viitoare planificată.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"choose-a-fermion-to-qubit-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Choose a fermion-to-qubit encoding {#3-choose-a-fermion-to-qubit-encoding}"
msgstr "3. Alege o codificare fermion-qubit {#3-choose-a-fermion-to-qubit-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit is still fermionic, and that is the point at which this package earns its place in the workflow. A [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") carries no assumption about how modes become qubits, so the encoding is a *synthesis-stage* choice rather than something baked into the ansatz. That is what this package adds over ffsim’s own Qiskit gates, which are specific to the Jordan-Wigner transformation.\n"
msgstr "Circuitul este încă fermionic și tocmai aici pachetul acesta își câștigă locul în fluxul de lucru. Un [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") nu presupune nimic despre cum devin modurile qubiți, deci codificarea este o alegere din *etapa de sinteză*, nu ceva încorporat în ansatz. Aceasta este ceea ce adaugă acest pachet față de porțile Qiskit proprii ale ffsim, care sunt specifice transformării Jordan-Wigner.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For Jordan-Wigner alone you would not need this detour: ffsim ships [`UCJOpSpinBalancedJW`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.qiskit.UCJOpSpinBalancedJW.html#ffsim.qiskit.UCJOpSpinBalancedJW \"(in ffsim)\") and its siblings, which take a UCJ operator to a qubit circuit on their own. The reason to route the ansatz through a fermionic circuit is everything *else* an encoding can buy you. Local encodings, for instance, spend extra qubits to bound the Pauli weight of each term, which the [1D](1-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) and [2D](2-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) flow-set guides use to make a Trotter step’s two-qubit depth independent of the system size.\n"
msgstr "Doar pentru Jordan-Wigner nu ai avea nevoie de acest ocol: ffsim include [`UCJOpSpinBalancedJW`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.qiskit.UCJOpSpinBalancedJW.html#ffsim.qiskit.UCJOpSpinBalancedJW \"(in ffsim)\") și variantele sale, care transformă singure un operator UCJ într-un circuit de qubiți. Motivul pentru care treci ansatzul printr-un circuit fermionic este tot ce *altceva* îți poate oferi o codificare. Codificările locale, de exemplu, consumă qubiți suplimentari pentru a limita greutatea Pauli a fiecărui termen, lucru pe care ghidurile seturilor de flux [1D](1-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) și [2D](2-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) îl folosesc pentru a face adâncimea cu două qubiți a unui pas Trotter independentă de dimensiunea sistemului.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a UCJ ansatz specifically, the synthesis stage has to cover two kinds of gate:\n"
msgstr "Pentru un ansatz UCJ în mod specific, etapa de sinteză trebuie să acopere două tipuri de porți:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The diagonal Coulomb evolution.** [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") is already encoding-agnostic: [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") takes a mapper function, so the $e^{i \\mathcal{J}_k}$ layers lower through any encoding you can express as one. The [flow-set guides](1-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) show how to write one.\n"
msgstr "**Evoluția Coulomb diagonală.** [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") este deja agnostică față de codificare: [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") primește o funcție de mapare, deci straturile $e^{i \\mathcal{J}_k}$ coboară prin orice codificare pe care o poți exprima ca atare. [Ghidurile seturilor de flux](1-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) arată cum se scrie una.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The orbital rotations and the Slater-determinant preparation.** Neither an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") nor the [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") that the leading [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") and rotation fuse into (see below) is mapped to qubits as such. The [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") pass first breaks them down, in fermionic space, into [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gates on one or two modes each (and, for the preparation, an [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") of the reference), so any encoding that can map an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") handles them. Under Jordan-Wigner, the factors between adjacent modes become [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)objects at the qubit stage.\n"
msgstr "**Rotațiile orbitale și pregătirea determinantului Slater.** Nici [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\"), nici [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") în care fuzionează [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") de la început și rotația (vezi mai jos) nu este mapată ca atare pe qubiți. Pasul [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") le descompune mai întâi, în spațiul fermionic, în porți [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") pe unul sau două moduri fiecare (și, pentru pregătire, un [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") al referinței), așa că orice codificare care poate mapa un [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") le poate gestiona. Sub Jordan-Wigner, factorii dintre modurile adiacente devin obiecte [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)în etapa de qubiți.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The initialization.** The plugin for [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") is not parametrized by an encoding: it documents its assumption of an occupation-basis encoding with a 1-to-1 mode-to-qubit mapping, and emits gates directly on that basis. A different encoding needs its own plugin for it, and none ships yet.\n"
msgstr "**Inițializarea.** Pluginul pentru [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") nu este parametrizat de o codificare: documentează presupunerea unei codificări în baza de ocupare cu o mapare 1-la-1 între moduri și qubiți și emite porți direct în acea bază. O codificare diferită are nevoie de propriul plugin pentru aceasta și încă nu există niciunul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to transpile UCJ circuits under a non-Jordan-Wigner encoding is an open research question and this package provides the framework within which to develop such a pipeline. The remainder of this guide constructs the transpiler pipeline for the Jordan-Wigner encoding, equivalent to the one produced by [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\"), as an example.\n"
msgstr "Cum se transpilează circuitele UCJ sub o codificare non-Jordan-Wigner este o problemă de cercetare deschisă, iar acest pachet oferă cadrul în care se poate dezvolta un astfel de pipeline. Restul acestui ghid construiește, ca exemplu, pipeline-ul de transpilare pentru codificarea Jordan-Wigner, echivalent cu cel produs de [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\").\n"

